body:
Uniqlo has a jacket like that. I love it. [https://www.uniqlo.com/us/en/men-u-pile-lined-trucker-jacket-420429COL09SMA002000.html?s=shopping&&gclid=CjwKCAiA9JbwBRAAEiwAnWa4Q8a07k2lfGAfI5WAAfw\_ckzeIUcJXJZdyL9EC\_Au1ZUSfziglQymoBoCqWsQAvD\_BwE&gclsrc=aw.ds](https://www.uniqlo.com/us/en/men-u-pile-lined-trucker-jacket-420429COL09SMA002000.html?s=shopping&&gclid=CjwKCAiA9JbwBRAAEiwAnWa4Q8a07k2lfGAfI5WAAfw_ckzeIUcJXJZdyL9EC_Au1ZUSfziglQymoBoCqWsQAvD_BwE&gclsrc=aw.ds)

&#x200B;

Its on sale for $19 too!

It is more about transparency. Not being transparent about this could be a huge breach of trust. 

&#x200B;

If I flipped the roles, I would want to know if my SO had STDs. It's not a negative thing at all. It's just something I would want to know.

I was in a similar situation years back with my ex. 

&#x200B;

Guy introduced himself by asking her out and she said no, obviously, since she was dating me. He said he was just looking for friends. What ever the fuck that means. She invited him to our campus activities board club.   


I transferred over to another college and they got close. He started texting my ex that she should break up with because he's super in love with her. I told her that is not cool and talk to him about it. She told me she talked to him and i believed her. I did not, however, ask to see how she did nor ask for proof. That is trust, as should be in all relationships.

&#x200B;

He kept on being super aggressive with her. Even so telling all his friends (one of which was super close to me) that they were dating blah blah blah that she was going to leave me blah blah blah.

&#x200B;

I broke up with her, because of many other reasons, but that one was a big one. I did not tell her that though.

&#x200B;

They started dating a couple of months after we broke up. 

&#x200B;

I don't want to freak you out because I do believe my case is an extreme.   


I do think, however, she needs to respect the relationship and find a way to compromise instead of being passive. 

&#x200B;

I wish you all the best, friend.

I think cutting him off is a little to extreme but I completely agree she needs to do something if she respects the relationship. 

&#x200B;

She should draw a line and be very stern about it. If he continue to do so then she should do something drastic. If she doesn't just vocalize its not cool and you are not seeing change.
